  "result": "All three bugs are fixed:\n\n1. **`src/server/repositories/webhook-repository.ts`** — `updateEndpoint` used `input.enabled && {...}`, which silently dropped `enabled: false` from the update (since `false && x` is `false`, and spreading `false` is a no-op). Fixed to check `input.enabled === undefined`.\n2. **`src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts`** — the delivery run now checks `endpoint.enabled` and marks the delivery failed if the endpoint is switched off, instead of always \"delivering\" it.\n3. **`src/server/services/webhook-service.ts`** — `createWebhook` now counts *all* existing endpoints (not just enabled ones) against the plan's allowance, matching the already-correct action-level check in `create-webhook.ts`.\n\nThe enqueue path (`enqueueForOrg`) already correctly skipped disabled endpoints, so no change was needed there. Relevant tests still pass.",
